<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:56:11 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Trump admin 'destroying' US democracy with 'autocratic, terrorist version of Christian nationalism'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261021-trump-admin-destroying-us-democracy-with-autocratic-terrorist-version-of-christian-nationalism</link><description>
François Picard welcomes former US Assistant Secretary of Defense Jim Townsend and former US Air Force officer Michael (Mikey) Weinstein, founder and president of the Military Religious Freedom Foundation. Is American military power becoming an instrument of political and religious coercion, both at home and abroad? From the reported restrictions on Ukraine's access to Starlink satellite communications to the Trump administration's overtures towards Vladimir Putin and the growing controversy over religious ideology within the Pentagon, the two guests offer a stark assessment of the direction of American foreign and defence policy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a7272dc-cd98-11f1-85be-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-183123-184644-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a7272dc-cd98-11f1-85be-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-183123-184644-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5ce619dc-cd9c-11f1-a466-b98e12198941</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:11:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Trump exploits France riots to push false immigration claims ahead of midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261021-trump-uses-france-riots-to-push-false-immigration-claims-ahead-of-midterms</link><description>
Donald Trump and his inner circle are using unrest in France to push unsubstantiated claims blaming the riots on immigration, even showing French protest footage at midterm rallies. But there is no evidence linking immigration to the unrest, and it's prompted French President Emmanuel Macron to accuse world leaders of making “stupid comments” at France’s expense. Trump’s focus comes as Republicans face mounting pressure ahead of the midterms and his approval rating hits a reported record low.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d5be998-cd83-11f1-80ea-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-10-21-211315.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d5be998-cd83-11f1-80ea-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-10-21-211315.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a79e1cd4-cd85-11f1-8f33-95be71b0013f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:28:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Some Brazilians long associated with the left now shift towards Flavio Bolsonaro</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-some-brazilians-long-associated-with-the-left-now-shift-towards-flavio-bolsonaro</link><description>
In the first round of Brazil’s presidential elections, Flavio Bolsonaro got the most votes in 15 electoral districts in the North Zone of Rio de Janeiro, compared with 9 for Lula. This part of the city, long associated with the left and the social policies of Lula’s Workers’ Party, is now shifting towards former president Jair Bolsonaro’s son.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/449179c4-c088-11f1-8ee6-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277433106719.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/449179c4-c088-11f1-8ee6-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277433106719.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64824c74-cd5b-11f1-a1e4-a34bccdf8451</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:28:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Peter Zalmayev: 'Ukraine was showing all sorts of cards that Trump took away and gave to Putin'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-ukraine-was-showing-all-sorts-of-cards-that-trump-took-away-from-ukraine-and-gave-to-putin-1</link><description>
Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. And he warns, "I'm seeing, I'm smelling a Yalta II. I'm smelling another Munich (1938), where we're seeing appeasement of the aggressor." Ukraine faces the possibility that its sovereignty and security could become mere bargaining chips in an era Zalmayev describes as great-power "collusion". He delivers a forceful critique of the Trump administration's approach to Russia, arguing that Washington is weakening Ukraine's negotiating position while offering Vladimir Putin little incentive to abandon his maximalist demands. At stake, he suggests, are the cohesion of the transatlantic alliance, and the credibility of Western security commitments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd778d3c-cd5c-11f1-83c4-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-152316-153456-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd778d3c-cd5c-11f1-83c4-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-152316-153456-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e355ddbc-cd5c-11f1-83fb-51ed59c64853</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:44:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Concerns mount over artificial intelligence as Silicon Valley sees AI boom</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261021-concerns-mount-over-artificial-intelligence-as-silicon-valley-sees-ai-boom</link><description>
Tuesday, October 20 saw protests in more than 50 US cities against the rise of artificial intelligence. Demonstrators are calling for a moratorium on AI development, and the sentiment is shared by many: according to a recent study, 71 percent of Americans believe AI will lead to job losses. In the heart of Silicon Valley, record investment is now on a collision course with public fear and uncertainty. FRANCE 24's Pierrick Leurent and Valérie Defert report, with Wassim Cornet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/937a69a2-cd57-11f1-895b-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c8f2af1a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/937a69a2-cd57-11f1-895b-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c8f2af1a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65747f42-cca4-11f1-900a-a966862eede0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:15:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Pierrick LEURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump campaigns in deep-red states, fearing Democratic wave</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-campaigns-in-deep-red-states-fearing-democratic-wave</link><description>
The midterm elections are just two weeks away in the United States and Donald Trump is stumping for candidates in states that he won by double digits in 2024. Polls showing support for the Republican Party is slipping drastically, even in some deep red states. Story by Monte Francis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e9373b8-cd54-11f1-8f52-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-141659-141851-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e9373b8-cd54-11f1-8f52-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-141659-141851-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a4f1b6e8-cd54-11f1-bc39-ff6b676ce890</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:51:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>US sanctions on ICC are 'a shock' and 'unacceptable', Nobel peace laureate Navi Pillay says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261021-us-sanctions-on-icc-are-a-shock-and-unacceptable-nobel-peace-laureate-navi-pillay-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Navi Pillay described the US sanctions imposed on the International Criminal Court (ICC) hours after her award as "a shock" and "unacceptable". The South African judge also defended the UN commission of inquiry she chaired which concluded that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza: "We didn't come to that conclusion lightly." Rejecting claims that the ICC targets Africa, she said "the court is not selective".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36f02c16-cd30-11f1-bde0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/Untitled-Sequence-01-26.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36f02c16-cd30-11f1-bde0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/Untitled-Sequence-01-26.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38559cb0-cd32-11f1-998a-0996ab77a850</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:11:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>AI on the ballot? Voters in US midterms revolt against data centres</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261020-ai-on-the-ballot-voters-in-us-midterms-revolt-against-data-centres</link><description>
Two weeks out from the US midterm elections, there's bipartisan pushback against data centres that suck the water and power out of communities. Just two years ago, ChatGPT was still a brand-new thing, and AI was admired with awe by most voters. Like in 2024, the hot-button issue in swing constituencies remains inflation, or "the price of eggs". But anxiety over the end of the month is now coupled with anxiety over the end of the world.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aac402a4-ccb1-11f1-b252-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-20T17-55-58-249Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aac402a4-ccb1-11f1-b252-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-20T17-55-58-249Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2775fbcc-ccb2-11f1-b519-138e7a055033</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:45:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil’s presidential candidates push to have one another disqualified ahead of run-off</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261020-lula-campaign-seeks-disqualify-bolsonoro-from-brazil-presidential-vote-over-meta-interference</link><description>

 
Both candidates in Brazil's presidential election called for their rival's disqualification Tuesday over allegations of social media malfeasance, according to court filings. Left-wing President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva’s campaign said they will request the annulment of right-wing rival Flavio Bolsonaro's candidacy over alleged election interference by tech giant Meta, while Bolsonaro's team is accusing Lula of "abuse of power" in the mass sharing of government postings on WhatsApp.
 

 

</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3edd3e22-ccc3-11f1-9db3-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292009753736.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3edd3e22-ccc3-11f1-9db3-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292009753736.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">efadc6e2-ccc1-11f1-b58e-4fdd5d42c242</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:59:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3edd3e22-ccc3-11f1-9db3-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292009753736.jpg">© Andre Penner, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump campaigning in Republican strongholds amid slide in polls</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-campaigning-in-republican-strongholds-amid-slide-in-polls</link><description>
With the midterm elections fast approaching, US President Donald Trump is stumping for candidates in states that he won by double digits in 2024. Despite what he says, it’s a sign of what Trump and the Republican party are fearing: with polls showing GOP support slip drastically even in some deep red states. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f637b458-c269-11f1-a77a-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277064284536.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f637b458-c269-11f1-a77a-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277064284536.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b65da6a0-ccc1-11f1-947b-e7d993ab0c60</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:13:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterm elections: Trump approval rating falls to new low</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-us-midterm-elections-trump-approval-rating-falls-to-new-low</link><description>
With US President Donald Trump’s approval rating falling to a record low of 31%, Republicans are facing mounting concerns ahead of November’s midterm elections. Republicans are at risk of losing control of the House of Representatives, but how big could the Democrats’ gains be? FRANCE 24’s International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78964d88-cba7-11f1-83fd-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-17T212609Z-1651462827-RC285OA65KAS-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-KENTUCKY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78964d88-cba7-11f1-83fd-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-17T212609Z-1651462827-RC285OA65KAS-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-KENTUCKY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb02ff9e-cc95-11f1-a33f-379da1eeb20b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:22:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Alberta votes to remain part of Canada in victory for PM Carney</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-alberta-votes-to-remain-part-of-canada-in-victory-for-pm-carney</link><description>
Voters in oil-rich Alberta overwhelmingly backed remaining in Canada in the province's first-ever referendum on separation, with early results on Tuesday delivering a boost to Prime Minister Mark Carney’s push for national unity amid US President Donald Trump’s trade war and annexation threats.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71731502-cc49-11f1-9a03-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/1ad8bf591602a27cd0b017965aa19739c31b6e0e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71731502-cc49-11f1-9a03-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/1ad8bf591602a27cd0b017965aa19739c31b6e0e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b7e6a11c-cbcb-11f1-949c-03fe4f459215</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:45:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71731502-cc49-11f1-9a03-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/1ad8bf591602a27cd0b017965aa19739c31b6e0e.jpg">© Megan Albu, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Four soldiers dead, dozens injured in fire at Canada military base</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-four-soldiers-dead-dozens-injured-in-fire-at-canada-military-base</link><description>
Four soldiers were killed and dozens injured in a fire at a military base in Alberta province, one of the worst peacetime tragedies to hit Canada's armed forces on home soil, Prime Minister Mark Carney said Sunday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e49123dc-a087-11f1-8dc3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T163056Z-1186857443-RC2R3NAM318W-RTRMADP-3-CANADA-DEFENSE-ICEBREAKERS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e49123dc-a087-11f1-8dc3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T163056Z-1186857443-RC2R3NAM318W-RTRMADP-3-CANADA-DEFENSE-ICEBREAKERS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1113910a-cbb3-11f1-9294-0daba255a691</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:25:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil court orders Meta to prove it gives Lula, Bolsonaro campaign content equal treatment</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-brazil-court-orders-meta-prove-gives-lula-bolsonaro-campaign-content-equal-treatment</link><description>

 
Brazil’s top electoral court has given Meta 24 hours to prove it is treating campaign content from incumbent President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and Senator Flavio Bolsonaro equally on its online platforms, threatening a daily fine for noncompliance. The ruling follows allegations from Lula's campaign that the social media giant is suppressing Lula’s campaign content ahead of Sunday’s closely contested presidential runoff.
 

 

 

</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68cd318a-cb9a-11f1-b04b-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292009828544.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68cd318a-cb9a-11f1-b04b-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292009828544.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c3c284fa-cbc2-11f1-8230-6f7aedcd9302</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:16:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68cd318a-cb9a-11f1-b04b-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292009828544.jpg">© Andre Penner, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil's Lula, Bolsonaro clash in bitter debate ahead of election run-off</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-brazil-lula-bolsonaro-debate-election-runoff</link><description>
Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and right-wing senator Flavio Bolsonaro traded personal attacks in a heated presidential debate on Sunday, a week before a closely contested run-off. The rivals accused each other of lying and corruption while clashing over the economy, security and healthcare ahead of the October 25 vote.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bb634d24-cb65-11f1-950d-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/67f4a5def68caac4535e07c4b807d8481ff0047aw.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bb634d24-cb65-11f1-950d-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/67f4a5def68caac4535e07c4b807d8481ff0047aw.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d5a948b6-cb6d-11f1-a0c3-eb52fc046c1d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:42:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bb634d24-cb65-11f1-950d-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/67f4a5def68caac4535e07c4b807d8481ff0047aw.jpg">© Sebastiao Moreira, EFE</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Canadian military base fire kills at least four, injures dozens</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-canada-military-base-fire-four-dead-39-hospitalised</link><description>
Four Canadian service members were killed and 39 people hospitalised after a fire broke out during military training at a base in Alberta on Saturday, officials said. Premier Danielle Smith said Sunday that at least 19 patients were in critical condition, with some suffering severe burns requiring prolonged intensive treatment.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f386ca2a-cb40-11f1-afbe-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26291249437617.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f386ca2a-cb40-11f1-afbe-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26291249437617.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ec3091a-cb3c-11f1-9ebd-e74f49cd2097</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:16:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f386ca2a-cb40-11f1-afbe-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26291249437617.jpg">© John Ulan, The Canadian Press</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Atlanta’s iconic tavern marks Georgia’s past with an eye on future as midterms approach</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-atlanta-iconic-tavern-marks-georgia-past-eye-future-midterms-approach-ossoff-collins</link><description>
Since it was established in 1956, Manuel’s Tavern in Atlanta has hosted legendary Democratic leaders while its founder played a key role in the city’s move from a Republican to Democratic stronghold. With the state’s Democratic Senator Jon Ossoff leading the polls in the midterms amid rumours of a future presidential run, the tavern is once more at the heart of the political action.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa2b4854-c967-11f1-a45e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/manuels-main.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa2b4854-c967-11f1-a45e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/manuels-main.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08f298ba-c968-11f1-84d4-7b0775633891</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:15:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa2b4854-c967-11f1-a45e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/manuels-main.jpg">© Branden Camp, AP</source><dc:creator>Leela JACINTO</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Rubio says Trump to 'analyze' global impact of Russia sanctions during pause</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-rubio-says-trump-russia-sanctions-waiver-designed-to-analyze-global-impact</link><description>
US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Saturday that US President Donald Trump’s decision to waive sanctions and tariffs on Russia would last 60 days, as the move drew bipartisan criticism and raised fears in Ukraine that Washington could ease further restrictions on Moscow.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b46d8a0-c7e7-11f1-819e-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/dcd8c89867be21a42771dcc4bb966f7a0278e690.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b46d8a0-c7e7-11f1-819e-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/dcd8c89867be21a42771dcc4bb966f7a0278e690.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">25029a10-ca9d-11f1-aa47-9186c059e688</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:39:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b46d8a0-c7e7-11f1-819e-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/dcd8c89867be21a42771dcc4bb966f7a0278e690.jpg">© Mark Schiefelbein, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>‘Standing up for democracy’: Atlanta ‘No Kings’ rally draws Trump critics ahead of midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-standing-up-for-democracy-atlanta-no-kings-rally-draws-trump-critics-ahead-of-us-midterms</link><description>
“No Kings, Vote Now” was the theme of a rally in Atlanta, one of many organised across the US on Saturday. While many demonstrators denounced US President Donald Trump’s policies, organisers said the rally was aimed at getting out the vote in the November 3 midterm elections and protecting democracy in America.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5ef54b2-ca8c-11f1-b97e-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290606906702.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5ef54b2-ca8c-11f1-b97e-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290606906702.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">174d7436-ca8d-11f1-b7da-d91d395a4215</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:50:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5ef54b2-ca8c-11f1-b97e-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290606906702.jpg">© Jose Luis Magana, AP</source><dc:creator>Leela JACINTO</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Embattled new White House Press Secretary Zacharia 'let go' from her role</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261016-embattled-new-white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-let-go-from-her-role</link><description>
A White House Press official said Friday that Secretary ​Katie Zacharia was "let go" from her role after US President Donald Trump signaled she was on her way out, a week after he picked her for the post. Zacharia's credentials as an attorney had come under scrutiny and she admitted to not having passed the bar in an interview with Fox News on Thursday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1595f724-c98b-11f1-b0e5-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T175004Z-783479373-RC2F2OAQ1A0D-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-WHITEHOUSE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1595f724-c98b-11f1-b0e5-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T175004Z-783479373-RC2F2OAQ1A0D-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-WHITEHOUSE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">476cb294-c97a-11f1-a627-09489461aad5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:57:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1595f724-c98b-11f1-b0e5-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T175004Z-783479373-RC2F2OAQ1A0D-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-WHITEHOUSE.jpg">© Kevin Lamarque, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>'Thanks a lot, Trump': Wyoming conservatives divided ahead of US midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261016-thanks-a-lot-trump-wyoming-conservatives-divided-ahead-us-midterms</link><description>
Famous for its cowboy culture, Wyoming is the least populated, the most rural and the most conservative of all the US states. With two weeks to go until the midterm elections, our reporters James André and Sylvain Rousseau travelled across this Republican stronghold and found that the party of US President Donald Trump is deeply divided in the Cowboy State. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/149a27f8-c8b1-11f1-be6f-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/Reportersplus-FR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/149a27f8-c8b1-11f1-be6f-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/Reportersplus-FR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">848ff704-c8ac-11f1-86db-07741eb877d8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:48:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>James ANDRE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>No, this oil tanker didn’t carry Russian diesel to the United States</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261016-oil-tanker-carry-russian-diesel-united-states</link><description>
Following US President Donald Trump's October 9 announcement of an agreement signed with Russian President Vladimir Putin to import Russian diesel into the United States, a number of pro-Russian social media accounts began claiming that a Russian oil tanker was already carrying thousands of barrels of diesel to the United States. The ship was actually carrying fertiliser. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37f5e6f2-c8b0-11f1-b7e1-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/cover-tanker.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37f5e6f2-c8b0-11f1-b7e1-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/cover-tanker.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f81de89a-c8af-11f1-9a11-1719eb38e43c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:36:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37f5e6f2-c8b0-11f1-b7e1-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/cover-tanker.jpg">© X</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Teen shooter kills three children and teacher at Oregon elementary school</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead</link><description>
A 16-year-old gunman killed three children and a teacher at Silver Rail Elementary School in Bend, Oregon, on Thursday before being killed by a community member who pursued him inside, police said. Two other people were wounded in the shooting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bdabf8a-c8eb-11f1-84b0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288796036302.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bdabf8a-c8eb-11f1-84b0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288796036302.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">90f32458-c8e3-11f1-bc5d-3758f1fd4ff3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:58:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bdabf8a-c8eb-11f1-84b0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288796036302.jpg">© Joe Kline, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Fake AI images of protester go viral after woman punched at Trump's Ohio rally</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/fake-ai-images-of-protester-go-viral-after-woman-punched-at-trump-s-ohio-rally</link><description>
A protester who heckled US President Donald Trump at his midterm rally in Youngstown, Ohio, was physically assaulted and removed from the event, but fake AI-generated photos recreating the incident are going viral online. The images carry digital watermarks identifying them as AI-generated. While footage confirms the woman was punched, there is no evidence to support Trump's claim that the protester was "paid" to disrupt his speech, as he mocked her weight. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1970114-c8cc-11f1-8790-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-404d997e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1970114-c8cc-11f1-8790-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-404d997e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1951dde4-c8cb-11f1-9ae9-77f3b18a7a98</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:47:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Venezuela's Nicolas Maduro and wife Cilia Flores deny US torture charges as 'false accusations'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-venezuela-s-nicolas-maduro-and-wife-cilia-flores-deny-us-torture-charges-as-false-accusations</link><description>
Ousted Venezuelan president Nicolas Maduro and his wife Cilia Flores pleaded not guilty on Thursday to new torture charges brought against them by US authorities, calling them “false allegations". The couple has been held in a New York jail since their capture in early January and is facing a new indictment accusing them of conspiring to torture political opponents and US citizens.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/15d030e4-c8d0-11f1-9f77-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T173536Z-1131213406-RC2T3OAY8MGY-RTRMADP-3-USA-VENEZUELA-MADURO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/15d030e4-c8d0-11f1-9f77-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T173536Z-1131213406-RC2T3OAY8MGY-RTRMADP-3-USA-VENEZUELA-MADURO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d4fcee92-c8c3-11f1-b142-398a63ee7bee</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:11:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/15d030e4-c8d0-11f1-9f77-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T173536Z-1131213406-RC2T3OAY8MGY-RTRMADP-3-USA-VENEZUELA-MADURO.jpg">© Jane Rosenberg, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'We're done': Ukraine resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries as 'only leverage' for peace talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-talks-1</link><description>
Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. As Zelensky declares Ukraine "done" with Trump's self-declared energy ceasefire and resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries, Zalmayev warns: "When you talk about the energy ceasefire, it presupposes two to be able to tango and to dance this dance." He challenges the legitimacy of Trump's unilateral announcement, made without agreement between Moscow and Kyiv, as Russia continues attacking Ukraine's energy infrastructure. Yet he cautions that Zelensky may need tactical restraint to preserve vital US support. Zalmayev also examines Western sanctions, frozen Russian assets, and Washington's pursuit of economic normalization with Moscow without meaningful Russian concessions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58af4524-c8af-11f1-8d33-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-130211-131029-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58af4524-c8af-11f1-8d33-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-130211-131029-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a36ed962-c8af-11f1-bc01-231790081c82</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:14:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Midterms 2026: Georgia's Ossof-Collins showdown lies at the heart of the battle for US Senate</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-2026-midterms-georgia-s-ossof-collins-showdown-lies-at-the-heart-of-the-battle-for-us-senate</link><description>
In Georgia, Democrat Jon Ossoff’s seat is one of the key contests in the US mid-term elections on 3 November. In this state, which was won by Donald Trump in 2024, the incumbent senator is facing Republican Mike Collins. Our reporter Leela Jacinto visited Manuel’s Tavern, a historic bar in Atlanta that has been frequented for decades by Democratic politicians. There, patrons watched the debate between the two candidates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1db4a806-c8aa-11f1-b400-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/minia-midterms-en.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1db4a806-c8aa-11f1-b400-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/minia-midterms-en.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3dd8867a-c8aa-11f1-9f95-271d8c4d2a7e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:14:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump cancels livestreaming of Fort Hood shooter’s firing squad execution</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-fort-hood-shooter-s-firing-squad-execution-will-not-be-livestreamed-trump-says</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said Thursday that he was cancelling plans to livestream the firing squad execution of a convicted military base shooter – a project that had sparked outrage in the United States. Nidal Hasan is scheduled to be executed on December 3 at Fort Hood in Texas, where he killed 13 people in 2009.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24ad22c2-c40f-11f1-afd3-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-PORTADA-EEUU-TRUMP-FRAUDE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24ad22c2-c40f-11f1-afd3-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-PORTADA-EEUU-TRUMP-FRAUDE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">367fca22-c8a6-11f1-90b1-732149be7923</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:58:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24ad22c2-c40f-11f1-afd3-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-PORTADA-EEUU-TRUMP-FRAUDE.jpg">© Alex Brandon, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Observers</category><title>Haiti: Capoeira classes aim to promote peace</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261015-haiti-capoeira-classes-promote-peace</link><description>
An association in Haiti is organising capoeira classes – an Afro-Brazilian martial art – in an attempt to reduce community violence and promote social reintegration. The Observers team spoke to its founder, Rodney Jean Marc, who said their doors are open to everyone, “even children in armed gangs”. The initiative takes place as the country's security situation has worsened in recent years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f47782f4-c89c-11f1-b27c-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-horizontale-sans-titre-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f47782f4-c89c-11f1-b27c-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-horizontale-sans-titre-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">471f7486-c89c-11f1-9e1e-ed17d87d24e7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:25:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump waives fresh sanctions against Russia in new low for Ukraine ties</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-trump-waives-fresh-sanctions-against-russia-in-new-low-for-ukraine-ties</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Friday put a sweeping package of sanctions and tariffs targeting Russian energy revenues on hold, saying the waiver was in the country's national interest. The relationship between Washington and Kyiv has been fraying since Trump struck a deal with Moscow to ease sanctions in exchange for Russia flooding the global market with diesel to bring down fuel costs.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a984948-c9e4-11f1-96bf-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2b8590e71b10a5e0f32dc9660d16df91306b4658.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a984948-c9e4-11f1-96bf-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2b8590e71b10a5e0f32dc9660d16df91306b4658.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">306bf100-c88e-11f1-893d-272076fb8a53</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:47:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a984948-c9e4-11f1-96bf-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2b8590e71b10a5e0f32dc9660d16df91306b4658.jpg">© Brendan Smialowski, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
